Description: Wait for client dmabufs' implicit fences before using them
 A client that doesn't use linux-drm-syncobj may commit a dmabuf its GPU
 is still rendering into. Same-GPU sampling waits for the implicit fence,
 but another GPU's driver may not: on hybrid laptops NVIDIA composites a
 monitor on its port with windows Mesa rendered on the Intel iGPU, and
 half-drawn frames showed up as tearing inside windows. As mutter does,
 hold such a commit (on the existing acquire-point wait path) until the
 dmabuf is readable, releasing the buffer if a later commit replaces it.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: not yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
